Decomposition : Apply the tableaux rules until we find an intepration that guarantees we cannot find it. 
Rules :   If C and D belongs to A then add C(x), D(x) to A
	If C or D belongs to A then add either C(x) or D(x) to A
	If exists r.c(x) belongs to A then add r(x,y), C(y) to A
	If for all r.C belongs to A then add C(y) to A

Note that there is no rule to handle negation! It appears as the last item of the decomposition. 
A set of assertions A is saturated of no rule is applicable any more to it and Closed if there exists an Obvious contradiction. It is Open if its not closed. 
